module applied_sum_arm.pos_1

// A `match` ON A PLAIN SUM WITH A PAYLOAD -- the control that named the axis,
// and the half that works.
//
// It is here because of what it PROVED rather than what it does: this shape was
// accepted throughout, while the same shape over an `Option[int]` was refused as
// "this arm names a variant of a different sum". Two shapes, one payload each,
// one arm each -- so the axis was neither the payload nor the arm. It was the
// APPLICATION: `Some` is registered under the generic `Option` and a scrutinee
// of type `Option[int]` is a different TyId, which the door compared directly.
//
// Its pair `neg_1.nv` holds the applied case, which is refused BY NAME now
// instead of being described wrongly.

type Box enum Empty | Full(int)

fn from_box(b Box) -> int => match b {
    Full(v) => v
    Empty => 0
}

fn main() {
    println(from_box(Full(7)))
    println(from_box(Empty))
}
